{
  "1145093": "deepmerge-ts stack exhaustion (GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx) via mailparser->html-to-text->deepmerge-ts@7.1.6. Exploit requires an attacker to control both merge inputs with a matching circular key path; html-to-text only uses deepmergeCustom internally to merge its own fixed default options with a caller-supplied options object, and we call mailparser's simpleParser() with no options, so no attacker-controlled object graph ever reaches the merge. An `overrides` pin to html-to-text@10.0.1 was tried but breaks CDK's NodejsFunction Lambda bundling (its generated bundling package.json doesn't carry the `overrides` field, so `npm ci` sees the lockfile's overridden version as out of sync with mailparser's own pinned dependency and fails). Remove once mailparser bumps its exact html-to-text pin past 10.0.0."
}
